To explicitly load a shared library in unix (Solaris/HP-UX), there is dlopen().  To
close it, you can call dlclose().  Run man dlopen for more information.  Normally
installation of software does not overwrite shared libraries that belong to the
system.  If it does, that is a serious problem.  On most Unix systems, you can set
a library path (like PATH) that includes the location of all interested libraries.
In this regard, it is not necessary to overwrite any existing libraries.  You just
have to change the library path instead.



