The 1024 limit for UNIX termcap entries has been there since
day one. It's nothing new. 

Check the end of the termcap entry for something like
tc=vt100. For example

 db|vt300|vt300-am|Digital VT300:\
        :hs:es:ts=\E[1$}\E[;H\E[K:fs=\E[0$}:ds=\E[1$}\E[;H\E[K\E[0$}:\
        :rf=/usr/share/lib/tabset/vt300:\
        :tc=vt100:

Here the capabilites hs,es,ts and rf are defined and the other 
capabilites for this terminal are to be found in the vt100
entry.

Hope this helps

  Finnbarr



