AlphaStation 255/233Mhz? I have one that has AlphaBIOS on it. Is that
the CMOS you are referring to.

My understanding is the AlphaStations are "half-flashed". That means
that they do not have the full ARC/SRM console prompt most other Alphas
do. What you need in order to get DUNIX running is the firmware update
to switch the machine from AlphaBIOS to the SRM console.

Sooo... First thing you need to do is get your hands on the firmware
files. If you have the full DUNIX CD set, there should be a Firmware CD
on it. Follow the appropriate instructions on the CD for your machine
(CD should be Windows readable). If not, firmwares and instructions can
be found at:

	http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/

Again, get the right files/instructions for your machine. Especially the
release notes. It looks like you'll want to do a combination of the
AlphaBIOS update with the SRM console files. Or best guess. I've never
tried, but have heard it can be done. The closest I have come is putting
Linux on my machine, but it's able to use AlphaBIOS as is.

Beyond that, the rest should be a straightforward DUNIX install...
Assuming you have not added any unsupported hardware to the machine.

Good luck...
