Hi Matt,
   You need to make sure you have your OSF-BASE and OSF-USR licenses
installed from your License PAK (Product Authorization Key).  See
"Licensing your software" in the installation manual for details.

   A quick test is to run "lmf list" from the command line (as root) and
ensure that both OSF-BASE and OSF-USR licenses show up. You can also
just fire up License Manager form the GUI.   If either OSF-BASE or
OSF-USR don't show up, add them in. One caveat though.  If after
installing, you still get the same response, check the "key options" on
the OSF-BASE License PAK.  If it has "MOD_UNITS" you may have to up the
"number of units" to get things to where you can log on as someone else
(see man page for lmf).

Martin



